[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Data Fetching Strategies, Caching, and Revalidation in Next.js"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"Next.js extends the native JavaScript fetch API to allow developers to configure caching and revalidation behavior for each fetch request on the server. Understanding these strategies is critical for building high-performance, scalable web applications."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"1. Static Data Fetching (Default Caching)"},{"order":4,"type":"paragraph","text":"By default, Next.js automatically caches the returned values of fetch requests indefinitely in the Data Cache. This is akin to Static Generation (SSG)."},{"order":5,"type":"code","text":"async function getData() {
  const res = await fetch('https://api.example.com/data');
  return res.json();
}"},{"order":6,"type":"subheading","text":"2. Server-Side Rendering (Dynamic Fetching)"},{"order":7,"type":"paragraph","text":"To fetch fresh data on every single request, bypassing the cache entirely (similar to Server-Side Rendering or SSR), you can pass the { cache: 'no-store' } option to the fetch function."},{"order":8,"type":"code","text":"async function getDynamicData() {
  const res = await fetch('https://api.example.com/data', { cache: 'no-store' });
  return res.json();
}"},{"order":9,"type":"subheading","text":"3. Time-based Revalidation"},{"order":10,"type":"paragraph","text":"When you want to cache data but update it after a specific amount of time, you can use the next.revalidate option in fetch. This implements Incremental Static Regeneration (ISR)."},{"order":11,"type":"code","text":"async function getCachedData() {
  const res = await fetch('https://api.example.com/data', {
    next: { revalidate: 3600 },
  });
  return res.json();
}"},{"order":12,"type":"subheading","text":"4. On-Demand Revalidation"},{"order":13,"type":"paragraph","text":"Data can also be revalidated on-demand based on an event (such as a form submission or webhook) using Next.js Server Actions or API routes with revalidatePath or revalidateTag."},{"order":14,"type":"code","text":"async function getTaggedData() {
  const res = await fetch('https://api.example.com/posts', {
    next: { tags: ['posts'] },
  });
  return res.json();
}"},{"order":15,"type":"bullet_point","text":"cache: 'force-cache' is the default behavior, storing responses in the Data Cache."},{"order":16,"type":"bullet_point","text":"cache: 'no-store' fetches fresh data on every request and disables caching."},{"order":17,"type":"bullet_point","text":"next: { revalidate: seconds } sets the cache lifetime in seconds for ISR."},{"order":18,"type":"bullet_point","text":"next: { tags: [...] } allows purging cache groups on-demand using revalidateTag."}]
